`dashboard/packages/core/src/sheets/` is ported from GenOffice's spreadsheet
domain (`apps/sheets/src/domain` and the pivot definition types from
`apps/sheets/src/gateway/xlsx-pivot.ts`). It is the pivot-table engine, the
chart model and recommender, flash fill, range sorting, formula reference
shifting, the A1 address reader and the in-memory workbook the rest of them are
written against.

Why it is here rather than written again: Polaris' spreadsheet is built on
Univer, whose open edition ships the grid, the formulas and the formatting and
deliberately does not ship pivot tables, charts or flash fill - those are what
its makers sell. GenOffice had written exactly those, as pure TypeScript with
no framework in it, under a licence that permits this.

The Apache 2.0 licence text is at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.
The files carry a header saying where they came from; their behaviour is
unchanged, and their formatting follows this repository's conventions.
